Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Copy private PE sections into anonymous image memory

Android denies restoring execute permission on modified private file mappings.
Mapping executable initially is insufficient: CLR temporarily makes its native
image sections writable to apply fixups before restoring executable protection.

Use the existing read-based image loading path for private PE sections. Keep
shared mappings file-backed, and leave ordinary data mappings unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -2615,7 +2615,10 @@ static NTSTATUS map_file_into_view( struct file_view *view, int fd, size_t start, size_t size,
 
     /* only try mmap if media is not removable (or if we require write access),
        and if alignment is correct */
-    if ((!removable || (flags & MAP_SHARED)) && host_addr == map_addr && host_size == map_size)
+    /* Private image pages may be patched and made executable again. Android
+     * rejects this for dirty file mappings; use the existing copy path. */
+    if ((!(view->protect & SEC_IMAGE) || (flags & MAP_SHARED)) &&
+        (!removable || (flags & MAP_SHARED)) && host_addr == map_addr && host_size == map_size)
     {
         if (mmap( host_addr, host_size, prot, flags, fd, offset ) != MAP_FAILED)
             return STATUS_SUCCESS;
